cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Ingence"
abstract: >-
  Ingence is a read-only indexing and inference engine for scientific filesystems, with a local
  Dashboard for exploring them. It reads files’ names, metadata and contents where they already
  sit, and interprets them through two editable, versioned sources: a Dictionary, which defines
  what the words in names and files mean, and a Rulebook, the engine’s interpretive logic, which
  turns that evidence into proposals about how files relate. The Dashboard lets you search and
  browse what is there, what could not be read, and what the engine concluded and why; where the
  rules cannot decide, it asks you.
